# NO DOCUMENT EVER ENTERS THIS REPOSITORY.
#
# github.com/magpiexyz-lab/FraudShield is PUBLIC. Twenty of the forty documents
# in this evaluation are forged financial records; three of those were built
# specifically to defeat metadata forensics. Committing them would publish a
# working set of forgery templates and a labelled map of what gets past a fraud
# detector -- from the repository of a fraud-detection product.
#
# The documents live in a private Supabase Storage bucket. This file is the last
# line of defence, not the first: the rule is that they are never copied into
# the working tree at all. run.mjs streams them to a temp directory outside the
# repo for exactly as long as a scan takes.
#
# Deny everything, then re-allow the few text artefacts that are meant to be
# tracked. An allowlist, because a denylist of extensions is one unfamiliar
# format away from leaking.
*
!.gitignore
!README.md
!labels.csv
!labels-images.csv
!labels-retry.csv
!labels-v2.csv
!labels-v2-images.csv
!run.mjs
!results/
!results/*.md
!results/*.csv
!results/.gitkeep
